STUDY OBJECTIVE
To better understand how to use OOP by applying its four pillars: Abstraction, Encapsulation, Inheritance, and Polymorphism.

MINI-PROJECT OBJECTIVE
To create any number of cars or trucks (with the flexibility to easily add new vehicle classes) and list all registered vehicles along with a rental simulation.

HOW IT WORKS

Vehicle: It acts as a blueprint for each vehicle, serving as the abstract Parent Class.

Cars: A Child Class used to define the specific rules and attributes for cars.

Trucks: A Child Class used to define the specific rules and attributes for trucks.

FleetManager: The class responsible for managing the array of registered vehicles. It handles the manual dynamic expansion of the array, adds new vehicles, and displays the fleet list.

Main: The class responsible for interacting with the user, collecting inputs, and handling validations.

HOW TO RUN
Run the Main class and type a number between 1 and 4 in the console:
1 - Register a new car
2 - Register a new truck
3 - List all registered vehicles and simulate rental values
4 - Quit the application